invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_point.c
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: the doubling sets Y3 = 1 under an if on Z1's zero mask in place
  of the masked move. Z1 is a coordinate of a multiple of a secret
  scalar, so the branch reads a secret, and lint-wide-multiply counts
  the branch the compiler emits for it: p256_wide_point.c's count goes
  past its ceiling of 3 under both 64-bit specs.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_cmov(&y3, &p256_wide_fe_one_mont, p256_wide_fe_zero_mask(&a->z));
--- new
    if (p256_wide_fe_zero_mask(&a->z) != 0) {
        y3 = p256_wide_fe_one_mont;
    }
